==Battleground==
*1 [[Croakley]] spawns as the boss after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>.
*1 [[The Face]] spawns.
*5 [[Wall Doge]]s spawn after 26.67 seconds<sup>800f</sup>, delay 13.33~16.67 seconds<sup>400f~500f</sup>.
*5 [[Wall Doge]]s spawn after 106.67 seconds<sup>3,200f</sup>, delay 20~23.33 seconds<sup>600f~700f</sup>.
*5 [[Wall Doge]]s spawn after 200 seconds<sup>6,000f</sup>, delay 26.67~30 seconds<sup>800f~900f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Wall Doge]]s spawn after 320 seconds<sup>9,600f</sup>, delay 33.33~36.67 seconds<sup>1,000f~1,100f</sup>.
*1 [[Berserkory]] spawns after 80 seconds<sup>2,400f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Berserkory is likely the biggest threat in the stage with his level 12 wave attacks, somewhat complicated by Croakley's 60-second slow ability. As The Face has roughly 2 million health and spawns at the start, most strategies must focus on endurance since they cannot hope to defeat it and destroy the base within 80 seconds. Once he is dealt with, the remaining enemies can be slowly whittled down, with Wall Doges posing little threat on their own. In some cases, it may be necessary for the base to tank some of Croakley's attacks.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Octopus Cat]] - Octopus Cat is typically the most accessible Wave Shield available at this point and will assist greatly on lower difficulties. If combined with other anti-Red specialists, Berserkory can be quite literally erased.
*[[Fish Cat (Normal Cat)|Island Cat]]/[[Crazed Fish Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Island Cat]]/[[Li'l Fish Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l Island Cat]] - Generic anti-Red melee specialists with the Strong Ability, they'll be the mainstay of frontline fighting, as they can tank a few Berserkory attacks and deal substantial damage. Even outside of his targeted trait, Manic Island is still viable as a cheap general purpose unit.
*[[Apple Cat (Super Rare Cat)|iCat]] - Having a 100% chance to freeze Red enemies for 2 seconds, iCat is essential for paralyzing Berserkory, buying other units a chance to whittle at him without suffering from his wrath.
*[[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] - A fast and powerful melee rusher with extreme damage, Bahamut is a core element of many strategies, as he will usually be the main damage source, especially in 4-crown where many otherwise useful units are locked out.
*[[Healer (Special Cat)|Healer Cat CC]] - For those who have his True Form from the [[Merc Storia Collaboration Event|Merc Storia]] collab, Healer's area attacks can perma-freeze any non-Metal enemy with the help of some Freeze Up combos (3x Sm, or 1x M + 1x Sm), and as a special unit, he is available in 4-crown. Proper timing, however, is needed so he can get the drop on The Face and Berserkory and disable them before he can be hit, as otherwise his long cooldown means the next won't come in time to save the attempt.

